    "file": "examples/apps/quorum/src/main/java/net/terminalvalue/quorum/raft/ReplyRule.java",
    "startLine": 14,
    "code": "* sent and its next index past them; on a refusal, the next index moves back by one, and the next request tries from\n* one entry earlier, until the consistency check passes.\n*\n* <p>An acceptance is the follower's own word on what it holds, and the record follows it whenever it comes, a late\n* or repeated one included: the next request then carries what the follower has already, which it accepts again. A\n* refusal of a request the leader has moved on from, or at an entry it knows the follower holds, does not back it up\n* again. The term check comes before this\n* rule, in {@link RoleMachine}: a reply from a newer term deposes the leader, and one from an older term, to a\n* request of an earlier term of its own, is dropped.\n*/\n   // ...\n       return switch (status) {\n           case AWAITED -> reply.accepted() ? transition(ANSWERED, ADVANCE) : transition(ANSWERED, BACK_UP);\n           case ANSWERED -> reply.accepted()\n                   ? transition(ANSWERED, ADVANCE) // the follower's own word on what it holds, late or not\n                   : unchanged(\"a refusal the leader has moved on from\");\n       };\n   }\n"
  },
